## Flow

```
auth ""  →  malloc allocates auth buffer at 0x804a008
        │
        ▼
service [str]  →  strdup() allocates at 0x804a018  (auth + 0x10)
        │
        ▼
service [str]  →  strdup() allocates at 0x804a028  (auth + 0x20)  ← non-null!
        │
        ▼
login  →  loads *(auth + 0x20)  →  non-null  →  JE not taken
        │
        ▼
system("/bin/sh")  ←  shell spawned as level9
```

**Alternatively with one long `service` string:**

```
auth ""  →  auth at 0x804a008
service [73+ 'a's]  →  strdup chunk at 0x804a018, data bleeds past 0x804a028
login  →  auth+0x20 non-null  →  shell
```

